{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And HaShem said: I have pardoned according to your word.</b> Meaning, I have not pardoned the sin definitively, but rather according to your words — that I shall not smite them at once — for the reasons He recorded in His statement, lest they say 'without being able' etc.; but in any case He will execute judgment upon them with length of patience, and this is the adjacent statement <b>all those men</b> etc. <b>if they see the land</b> etc. And His saying <b>as I live</b> means He swore by the life of the King, as it were; He also swore and said ״וְיִמָּלֵא כְבוֹד״ etc., meaning, so may the glory of HaShem fill the earth until this is done — and this too is an oath concerning the matter." "<b>Further</b>, it appears to explain the verse in this manner: <b>I have pardoned according to your word</b> — meaning, on account of your words, for you appeased My face, and on account of what is stated in Moses' words concerning the utterance of the nations, ״מִבִּלְתִּי יְכֹלֶת ה׳״ etc., and we explained there two ways: the first — that there is no other Elohim, heaven forbid; and the second — that He lacks the power against the inhabitants of the land. Therefore He said <b>but as I live</b> — meaning, corresponding to what they say that there is no existent who saves, heaven forbid, He said ״חַי אָנִי״; and corresponding to what they say that He lacks the power, heaven forbid, to stand against the inhabitants of the land, He said <b>and the glory of HaShem shall fill all the earth</b> — meaning, in the wondrous deed He will perform in the end against thirty-one kings, even though He will do this for the seed of Moses. And the intention of these words is to say that He did it only for the honor of Moses, who asked Him for forgiveness, and not out of concern for the utterance of the nations."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:09:13.999626209Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}